  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-6,4)$ and passes through the point $(-4,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-6,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x+6).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-4,8),$ we substitute $x=-4$ and $y=8$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8-4)^{2} & =4p(-4+6) \\\\ (4)^{2} & =4p\\cdot (2) \\\\ 16 & =8p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =8(x+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =8(x+6) \\\\ 16 & =8(x+6) \\\\ 2 & =x+6 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $-4.$",
